# Canonical area-characterization script for the STT protocol emulator.
#
# This file is a template: `make area` substitutes the @...@ markers with sed
# and writes the expanded script to build/<run>.ys, which is what Yosys actually
# runs.  The expanded script is kept, so every number in docs/area-study.md has
# a literal script next to it.  (Yosys does not expand shell variables inside
# .ys files, hence the substitution.)
#
# Markers:
#   @SOURCES@   space-separated Verilog sources
#   @TOP@       top module
#   @PRE@       optional commands to run before `hierarchy` (e.g. chparam -set)
#   @CHPARAM@   optional `-chparam NAME VALUE` pairs for the hierarchy pass
#   @FLATTEN@   `flatten` for the true total, empty to preserve hierarchy
#   @LIB@       absolute path to the typical-corner cmos5l liberty

read_verilog -sv -I@RTL@ @SOURCES@
@PRE@
hierarchy -check -top @TOP@ @CHPARAM@
proc; opt
@FLATTEN@
memory_map
opt -full
techmap; opt
dfflibmap -liberty @LIB@
abc -liberty @LIB@ -D 20000
setundef -zero
splitnets
opt_clean
stat -liberty @LIB@
